  "projectDescription": "The Stargazer Cyberdeck is a mobile writing station built around a Raspberry Pi controller, a compact keyboard, and a 7-inch touch display. Powered by an external source, this portable unit is ideal for focused work, especially during stargazing sessions.",
  "imagePromptSnapshot": {
    "tags": [
      "mobile cyberdeck",
      "writing focus",
      "star gazing",
      "compact keyboard",
      "7-inch display"
    ],
    "description": "Project idea: i want to create a mobile cyberdeck mainly for writing and looking at stars using the following parts: Keyboard: Hoopond Mechanical Keyboard, AK33 Green LED Backlit USB Cable Gaming Mechanical Keyboard, 82 key Compact Mechanical Gaming Keyboard with Anti-ghosting Keys for Gamers, Typists (Blue switch, Black)\nDisplay: Elecrow RC070 7inch 1024*600 LCD Display with IPS Touch Screen| Compatible with Windows/Raspberry Pi\nComputer: Raspberry Pi 3 Model B 1GB SC0022 64-bit Quad-Core Single Board Computer\n\nDesign notes: mobile cyberdeck, writing focus, star gazing, compact keyboard, 7-inch display\n\nElectrical components (current): Main Cyberdeck Controller (mcu, 85x56x17mm); Primary Touch Display (display, 165x125x13mm); 5x module: Input Keyboard, Pi Power Cable, Display Power Cable, Display Touch Data Cable +1 more; External Power Source (power, 150x75x25mm)\n\nMechanical/structural parts (current): 8x 3d_printed: Raspberry Pi Base Mount, Display Fixed Angle Bezel, Keyboard Recessed Tray, Pi USB Cable Clip +4 more; 2x structural: Case Lid Structural Panel, Main Base Structural Panel; 6x misc: M2.5 Mounting Screws for RPi, M3 Mounting Screws for Display, M3 Mounting Screws General, M3 Nuts +2 more\n\nAssembly: Main Base Structural Panel → Main Enclosure Case (affixed to base interior); Case Lid Structural Panel → Main Enclosure Case (affixed to lid interior); Raspberry Pi Base Mount → Main Base Structural Panel (M3 bolts and M3 nuts); Power Bank Retaining Tray → Main Base Structural Panel (M3 bolts and M3 nuts); Display Fixed Angle Bezel → Case Lid Structural Panel (M3 screws_general_mount into heat_set_inserts_m3); Keyboard Recessed Tray → Case Lid Structural Panel (M3 screws_general_mount into heat_set_inserts_m3); Pi USB Cable Clip → Main Base Structural Panel (adhesive or small screws); Display Power Cable Clip → Case Lid Structural Panel (adhesive or small screws); Display Touch Cable Clip → Case Lid Structural Panel (adhesive or small screws); HDMI Cable Clip → Case Lid Structural Panel (adhesive or small screws); Raspberry Pi Base Mount → Main Cyberdeck Controller (mount); Display Fixed Angle Bezel → Primary Touch Display (mount); Keyboard Recessed Tray → Input Keyboard (mount); Pi USB Cable Clip → Pi Power Cable (mount); Display Power Cable Clip → Display Power Cable (mount) (+3 more connections)"
  },
